pcg|n|The act of fleeing from danger, of evading harm, or of avoiding notice; deliverance from injury or any evil; flight; as, an escape in battle; a narrow escape; also, the means of escape; as, a fire escape. ; That which escapes attention or restraint; a mistake; an oversight; also, transgression. ; A sally. ; The unlawful permission, by a jailer or other custodian, of a prisoner's departure from custody. ; An apophyge. ; Leakage or outflow, as of steam or a liquid. ; Leakage or loss of currents from the conducting wires, caused by defective insulation.	a:hcr,77,1;134k,55,3;qne,52,3;5a0,46,13;1bl9,46,4;1ceq,36,3;txl,33,5;upw,31,8;172n,30,4;1707,29,5;1jaw,27,3;12n4,24,2;zw5,21,4;dwd,21,5;vqn,18,5~5a0,46,13;1vwu,16,9;upw,31,8;45o,3,5;12yo,4,5;1707,29,5;dwd,21,5;vqn,18,5;1c1k,6,5;txl,33,5;21ut,16,4;mss,7,4;26qc,1,4;172n,30,4;zw5,21,4	v:1fhr,60,1;pzg,39,5;nu0,39,3;y1k,38,14;pa,37,2;1o96,25,4;p6,23,7;1ldo,21,13;1n1l,19,3;1ldl,19,5;1o92,14,6;12n4,14,1;1o94,11,3;fve,7,3;1thv,6,4~y1k,38,14;1ldo,21,13;p6,23,7;1o92,14,6;1ldl,19,5;pzg,39,5;1thv,6,4;1o96,25,4;1o94,11,3;d69,1,3;nu0,39,3;1n1l,19,3;fve,7,3;pa,37,2;1fhr,60,1	V:2024,31,1;26uz,21,1;sgq,13,1;sks,6,3;ao6,5,1~sks,6,3;ao6,5,1;sgq,13,1;26uz,21,1;2024,31,1	n:17gl,79,4;hcr,77,1;1fhr,70,2;1g9u,42,3;4o8,33,2;134i,31,3;nsn,29,10;gnj,28,8;4u2,27,4;ruy,20,6;diu,19,2;m6x,19,5;1vkq,18,1;u7i,12,4;y1k,10,2~nsn,29,10;1td,1,10;gnj,28,8;ruy,20,6;m6x,19,5;17gl,79,4;4u2,27,4;u7i,12,4;134i,31,3;1g9u,42,3;1fhr,70,2;4o8,33,2;y1k,10,2;diu,19,2;1vkq,18,1	N:ww9,79,10;26v0,59,127;1qiz,58,4;1qzo,58,5;1jtg,57,4;233s,51,4;d2e,49,4;1toh,42,68;26uz,41,4;1y87,40,3;17uh,40,4;233t,38,4;2024,31,1;t5k,30,4;ao6,29,5~26v0,59,127;1toh,42,68;14cl,9,48;bw1,28,26;ww9,79,10;bvy,25,9;1qyp,15,6;1vce,25,6;1r5n,7,5;1ahn,14,5;1qzo,58,5;ao6,29,5;d2e,49,4;17uh,40,4;1qiz,58,4
